<.shell current={:page_actions}>
  <h1>Page actions</h1>
  <p class="lead">A page's own actions, when it has no sidebar to hold them.</p>

  <div class="demo">
    <h1 class="title">Incident hours</h1>
    <p class="lead">Incidents since a date, most hours first.</p>
    <.page_actions id="demo-page-actions">
      <:byline>Saved by Alex Chen on Nov 1, 2026.</:byline>
      <:action><.a href="#">Change report</.a></:action>
      <:action><.a href="#">Download CSV</.a></:action>
      <:action><.a href="#">Delete report</.a></:action>
    </.page_actions>
  </div>

  <h2>When to use</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      A page about one thing with no sidebar, such as a report: changing it, downloading it, deleting it.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>When not to use</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      A record page with a sidebar. Its actions go in the Actions list in its <a href={
        page_path(:detail_list)
      }>details</a>.
    </li>
    <li>
      Making something, such as Add activity. That's a button in a <a href={
        page_path(:heading_row)
      }>heading row</a>.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>How it works</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>It goes under the title and its lead, before the page's content.</li>
    <li>A byline first when the page has one: who made it, and when.</li>
    <li>
      Then the actions, side by side, each an arrow link. They wrap on a phone, and each takes
      a 44px row on a touch screen.
    </li>
    <li>The order is the Actions list's: change, send, reports, Open in D4H, Delete.</li>
    <li>
      Delete opens the <a href={page_path(:confirm_dialog)}>confirm dialog</a>, as it does in a sidebar.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>In the app</h2>
  <p>
    <code>&lt;.page_actions id="…"&gt;</code>
    with a <code>&lt;:byline&gt;</code>
    slot and one <code>&lt;:action&gt;</code>
    slot per link.
  </p>
</.shell>
